# Mountie's Microsoft Store listing: tools/store/listing.py fills Partner Center's Store listing page from this.
# Keys are the fields' labels as Partner Center shows them (listing.py survey lists them); a | b fills one box each.
@Listing Mountie
Language=English (United Kingdom)
Short description=Your drives, all in one place: SSH servers, disk images, RAM drives and your phone, as ordinary drives.
Description=<<END
Mountie puts the storage you use every day where you expect it: as drives in File Explorer.

• SSH and SFTP servers: your web server, a Raspberry Pi, a NAS, mounted as a drive letter and back again in a click. Passwords, keys and ssh-agent all work.
• Disk images: open ISO and VHD files as drives, without burning or unpacking anything.
• RAM drives and folders: a lightning-fast scratch drive, or any folder given a letter of its own.
• Your phone: with Mountie on your Android phone, share its photos, downloads and documents over Wi-Fi and open them here as a drive. Pairing is a QR code, and the phone asks before letting a computer in.

Mountie lives in the tray, remembers your drives, and can mount them for you when you sign in. It's made by Wallisoft, a small British developer, with Visualised.
END
Product features=Mount SSH and SFTP servers as drive letters | Open ISO and VHD disk images as drives | RAM drives and folder drives | Share your Android phone's storage over Wi-Fi | Pair a phone with a QR code, no passwords | Lives in the tray and mounts at sign-in
